00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:20.940
Historically, the marginalized people,

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.500
you call them as untouchables or Dalits,

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.630
they have been kept away from
the center of the knowledge.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.000
Once you are born into a caste,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.140
it is very difficult for
you to grow beyond that.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.690
You are stuck in that identity.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.410
Education is the best
way of liberating them.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.683
So that's how I chose to
work in education sector.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.090
The kind of education that

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.290
we are giving to the marginalized people

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.670
is going to change

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.840
not just the fate of these
communities in Telangana,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.543
but it is going to be the
source of inspiration,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.619
a source of hope, for all the
marginalized in this country.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:14.370
The greatest plight in India
is the system of caste.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.340
For generations of Indians,

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.940
the social code known as the caste system

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.960
has defined how people earn a living

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.760
and whom they marry.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.300
Although outlawed seven decades ago,

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.300
castes remain a significant factor

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.000
in deciding everything

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.790
from family ties and cultural traditions

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.673
to educational and economic opportunities.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.060
Dalits, people who are on the lowest

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.690
rung of the caste system,

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:43.660
constitute almost one-fifth
of India's population

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.299
of 1.3 billion.

00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:50.550
Not able to afford the high
tuition of private schools,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.670
many are forced to attend
government-funded institutions,

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.560
which in the past

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.500
have suffered from poor infrastructure,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.260
lower education standards

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.433
and high student-to-teacher ratios.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:04.573
But Dr. Praveen Kumar is
trying to change that.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.670
I'm currently working as you know

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.150
head of Telangana Social
Welfare Residential Schools.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.160
So totally about 400 schools I manage,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.370
they're all residential schools

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.050
for the students who are historically

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:26.643
marginalized, but talented and then poor.

00:02:31.132 --> 00:02:36.030
Of them, 60% are girls
and then 40% are boys

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.500
because girls are more marginalized

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.490
among the marginalized.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.763
Their voices are always suppressed.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.200
My approach to improve

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.330
the conditions in the schools has been

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.880
put your eyes and ears
on the ground always.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:52.810
Talk to the parents,

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:53.660
talk to the teachers,

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.283
talk to the students, you know.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.860
Stay in the schools and then
understand their problems,

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:00.693
their challenges,

00:03:00.693 --> 00:03:03.930
both in classrooms and in
the corridors and the dorms.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.520
Then go to the dining halls

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.140
and see what kind of food they're eating

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.220
and then go to their homes

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.750
and then what kind of food they're getting

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.675
and what kind of challenges
their parents have.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.850
One of the important changes

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.930
that I brought in after I took over

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.050
was to complete the transformation

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.820
of mother tongue to English medium,

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:28.000
because English medium, as I said,

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.550
English is the language of emancipation

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.770
and language that connects you

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.260
to the whole body of
knowledge in the world.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:39.098
So we had to train a lot of teachers.

00:03:39.098 --> 00:03:41.300
Refer to the dictionary also, OK,

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.800
and find out the new meanings.

00:03:45.946 --> 00:03:47.330
Hey Rachita, how are you?

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.214
Hi Sindhu, fine thank
you and how about you?

00:03:50.214 --> 00:03:51.370
I'm fine too, it's been a long time...

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.120
Identity is extremely important.

00:03:55.453 --> 00:03:57.840
There is a scientific
evidence to prove that,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.090
you know, your sense of identity is

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.060
extremely crucial to your growth

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.883
as a successful human being in your life.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.880
If you accept an identity
which is very humiliating,

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.980
which reminds you of very painful past,

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.845
I think that identity
will not help you to grow.

00:04:16.845 --> 00:04:19.430
I'm not saying that we
should forget your past.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:20.263
I'm not saying that.

00:04:20.263 --> 00:04:23.160
But that should not be the bubble

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.773
in which you must live always.

00:04:30.317 --> 00:04:33.240
SWAERO is an alternative identity.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.311
S stands for the state.

00:04:35.311 --> 00:04:40.161
W stands for welfare. Aero.
S,W and then aero is SWAERO.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.103
So the idea is that your
dreams have to be skybound.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.230
So, that is what we are trying to achieve

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.710
by changing the identities like, you know,

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:58.170
you say, I'm a SWAERO,
and I aim to be a doctor.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.630
I'm a SWAERO. I aim to
be a top-notch engineer.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:04.020
I'm a SWAERO. I aim to be a
top bureaucrat of this country.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.350
I'm a SWAERO. I want
to be a very good actor

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:09.760
or, you know, musician
in this, you know, world.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.350
So, these are the positive images

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.240
that are associated with identity.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.120
Just to give an example to you.

00:05:22.202 --> 00:05:25.330
See, in 2012, in our institutions,

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:28.900
we used to produce about
six doctors per year.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.810
But because of this
self-liberating ideology

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.713
of SWAEROism,

00:05:35.713 --> 00:05:38.420
we have this year,

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:43.410
we have produced about 189 doctors.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.380
This is phenomenal for any
poorest of the poor people.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:49.510
You know how difficult it is

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:52.090
to get into a medical
colleges in this country?

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.680
So but today,

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.020
because of this ideology,

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.323
the students have been
able to achieve this feat.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:05.580
Pujita has been a farm laborer.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.640
Her parents themselves

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.630
have been agricultural laborers,

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.690
and then this girl used
to sell vegetables,

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:14.160
but thanks to the residential
education institutions,

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.870
she came to the Gowlidoddi campus

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:20.850
and then she toiled very hard for one year

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:24.030
despite many problems.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.610
And today,

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.030
I'm so happy to share with you

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.420
that you know she is, she has joined

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:32.350
one of the prestigious medical colleges

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:34.650
in the state of Telangana,
Osmania Medical College

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.330
and then in future,

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.400
she hopes to be a gynecologist,

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.793
so this is the journey our
children are hoping for.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.970
Similarly, the Mount Everest expedition,

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.120
Mount Everest expedition,

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.480
we were, we are very fortunate enough

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.300
to place the youngest-ever female

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.990
in the history of this world

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:57.400
on the peak of Mount Everest.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:58.480
How did this happen?

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.360
It's all because of an ideology

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.160
that helps you to liberate yourself.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.310
We brought a lot of
extracurricular activities

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.110
and most of them got
institutionalized now.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.388
So for example, music.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.940
Similarly the games. We have
so many coaching academies,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.061
we have boxing academy,

00:07:22.061 --> 00:07:22.894
we have wrestling academy,

00:07:22.894 --> 00:07:24.760
we have handball academy.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:29.340
So we have kabaddi, that
traditional Indian sport.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.173
We have golf,

00:07:30.173 --> 00:07:31.573
we have introduced golf also.

00:07:31.573 --> 00:07:34.310
Golf is generally played
by so-called rich people,

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:36.380
but today even poorest of the poor people

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.093
also are being trained
in golf in our schools.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:44.320
So our intention has been
to give all 360 degrees,

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.100
you know, type of opportunities

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.980
to the students, so that whoever

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.380
is interested in whatever activity

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.803
they can go and then do it.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:55.543
Break the barriers.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:57.480
Break the fence,

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.650
at least mentally, because

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:03.370
poor people have been
programmed to be victims,

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.753
programmed to be subjugated,

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:11.040
programmed to be on the margins always,

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.853
programmed to feel inferior.

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.500
We wanted to change all that.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:16.430
There are certain games,

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.720
which are exclusive to rich people.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.910
There are certain languages,

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.690
which are exclusive to middle class

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:23.670
and upper middle class in this country.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.700
To put it in one word, the sole aim

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.120
of introducing all these
co-curricular activities

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.220
is to break the stereotypes,

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.470
which are recklessly
imposed on these people.

00:08:36.075 --> 00:08:39.890
They are stereotypes Dr.
Kumar knows all too well.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:40.723
Born a Dalit,

00:08:40.723 --> 00:08:42.310
his grandparents were laborers,

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:44.703
and access to the village
well was restricted.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.620
Dr. Kumar, credits his parents'

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.720
belief in the power of education

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.010
with helping him realize his aspirations.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.640
He went on to join the
Indian Police Service,

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:57.560
attended Harvard University

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:00.573
and then began pursuing
educational reforms back home.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.690
I attribute whatever I am today,

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.450
it's to my mother primarily.

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:08.220
They educated me in the village

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.450
although there were no good schools.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:13.130
So then I stayed in the
social welfare hostels,

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.640
the hostels which are
managed by the government

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.140
for the poorest of the poor kids.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:19.431
I passed with reasonably good grades.

00:09:19.431 --> 00:09:21.474
Then I went to university,

00:09:21.474 --> 00:09:22.998
and then I faced a worse
form of discrimination

00:09:22.998 --> 00:09:25.312
in the universities. Like
there were, you know,

00:09:25.312 --> 00:09:27.184
in those days I'm talking about,

00:09:27.184 --> 00:09:28.600
so the bathrooms and the toilets

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.688
were exclusively meant
for scheduled castes

00:09:30.688 --> 00:09:32.950
and scheduled tribes.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.770
We used to fight
discrimination on one hand

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:39.710
and then again try to excel in
academics day in and day out.

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:41.240
So that's how I came to education because

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.760
I deeply believe that education

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.180
is the only important weapon

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.840
that can really place the
poorest of the poor people

00:09:50.879 --> 00:09:55.879
from a very victimhood
orbit to a prosperous orbit.

00:09:57.136 --> 00:10:00.800
I think, in future, this is
going to be a game changer

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.993
for the for the marginalized
in this country.

